    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02746 is refunded to the rider in full, and no compensation is paid to the driver.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. POL-NS-01 requires all four of its conditions. The driver's 'I'm Here' event at 09:24:42 (EV-TRIP-02746) satisfies limb (a) only. Limb (b) fails: under POL-NS-02 the driver is deemed to have arrived only where the GPS trace holds at least three consecutive fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD-zone arrival radius with reported accuracy of 25 m or better, and the trace (EV-GPS-02746) contains zero qualifying in-geofence fixes (derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count = 0; zero runs). Limb (c) fails as well: the measured in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds (derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec = 0.0 s) against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (EV-TRIP-02746, platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180). POL-NS-06 therefore makes the cancellation fee not chargeable and refunds that line in full, whether or not the rider was present. The 6.7-minute wait timer in the trip record does not help the driver: POL-NS-01(c) runs the clock from GPS entry into the geofence, not from the arrival tap.\n\nThe driver's counterparty statement that he was 'at the pin for over six minutes' is his own account; it is contradicted by his own trace, it carries no weight multiplier, and it does not lift the POL-GEN-02 cap. His 'I'm Here' tap is a status he set, so it records only that he tapped. POL-NS-12 (platform-confirmed arrival) does not assist him because the arrival marker here is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO.\n\nThe rider's own track (EV-GPS-02746 rider_presence) places the rider about 837 m from the pin, but that does not change the outcome: POL-NS-06 refunds regardless of rider presence, and POL-NS-04 does not exonerate because the only chat message in the window is the driver's, so limb (a) is not met (limb (c) would also fail, the rider being well outside the 100 m STANDARD radius).\n\nOn the claims. The claims that the arrival tap was a false marker under POL-NS-05 are noted but not carried to a referral: POL-NS-05 turns on a specific pair of numbers - the driver's distance from the pin and his speed at the arrival timestamp - and the record supplies no driver position for 09:24:42, and the driver's trace minimum distance is 0.0 m, so a false-arrival finding is not established and no POL-NS-05(ii) referral is recorded. That point stays open for the platform's full-resolution stream. The anti-farming claims are accepted: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against completed_trips_30d of 126 (ratio 0.008, below 0.08), so POL-NS-07's withholding branch does not trip, and in any event POL-NS-07 pays nothing because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full.\n\nThe two claims about the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02746-01 (weight 0.0) were discarded by the referee for not naming the MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code; in any case that advisory only makes POL-NS-06(i) accumulation unavailable, and there is no in-geofence dwell to accumulate.\n\nNo escalation. Confidence is above the 0.70 POL-NS-09(a)/POL-GEN-02 floor; no artifact carrying the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08 - there is no clock skew (the nearest fix is within seconds of 09:24:42), no gap over 120 s (max_gap_sec 0.0, 71 fixes, 100% coverage), the chat log matches the trip record's chat_message_count of 1 with intact sequencing, and the SGD 4.50 fare line reconciles to platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd; the same rider and driver show no counterparty disputes; and POL-NS-02 resolves the only apparent conflict, namely the driver's tap against the trace.\n\nAmount. EV-FARE-02746 shows cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The full 4.50 is refunded. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically."
