    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The dispute is the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02746 (EV-FARE-02746: cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The rider is refunded in full.\n\nThe fee does not stand. Under POL-NS-01 a no-show fee is chargeable only if the driver both arrived inside the pickup geofence (limb (b), tested by POL-NS-02) and held position there for the free waiting period in force \u2014 180 seconds for this STANDARD-zone trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec) \u2014 measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and not from the arrival tap (limb (c)). The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-02746, weight 1.0, 100% coverage, 71 fixes, no gaps) fails both: derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count is 0 and the longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0 fixes over 0.0 seconds, while the driver track has a mean distance of 742.5 m from the pin (maximum 3,999.99 m) and recorded speeds of 32.8 to 62.9 km/h. No qualifying in-radius fix exists anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-02 finds the driver never arrived, POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails, and the effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds against the required 180 seconds \u2014 a shortfall of 180 seconds \u2014 so POL-NS-06 also refunds the fee in full.\n\nThe 'I'm Here' tap does not save the charge. POL-NS-05 makes the arrival marker false where the trace shows the driver travelling at 15 km/h or more at the tap, which it does, and recomputes the waiting clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix. There is no such fix anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05(ii) applies: the fee is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and the trip is recorded as a false-arrival event (see referrals). POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) does not apply: it needs the driver stationary for the required dwell within 400 m of the pin, and the track shows him driving (mean 742.5 m), not holding position. The driver's counter-statement that he 'was at the pin for over six minutes', and the in-app message 'im at the pickup point' at 09:25:02, are self-serving; the tap and the message record only that the driver said those things, and both are contradicted by the driver's own trace.\n\nNo driver compensation. POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full; it is not, so nothing is payable. The anti-farming check does not trip in any event (no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 126 = 0.008, below 0.08), and POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not engaged (no counterparty disputes; rider no_show_disputes_30d 0).\n\nThe rider's own conduct neither helps nor hurts the fee. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the only chat message is from the driver, not the rider (limb (a) fails), and the rider track (63 fixes, 833.9\u2013841.4 m from the pin) is outside the 100 m presence radius (limb (c) fails). The refund rests on the driver's own evidence, not on POL-NS-04.\n\nEscalation is not warranted. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d): the GPS has no gaps (max gap 0.0 s), the chat sequence is intact and matches chat_message_count 1, and the fare reconciliation is exact (4.50). POL-NS-09(e) therefore does not fire, and neither does POL-NS-09(b), because POL-NS-01(b) and POL-NS-05 state which record governs arrival. Confidence 0.9, the deciding facts being carried by artifacts at weight 1.0. The refund of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold (POL-GEN-05) and executes on issue.\n\nDiscarded claims. Two claims about traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02746-01 were discarded because they cited that weight-0.0 (MISSING) artifact without naming its issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. The advisory's absence is not relied on for this ruling; it means only that POL-NS-06(i) dwell accumulation cannot be run, which is immaterial because there is no in-geofence interval to accumulate."
